WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.299
If you want to challenge me to do some Dares
in a future video, stick around for the entirety

00:00:04.299 --> 00:00:11.440
video to find out how.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:15.030
Why have you taken me to this creepy place?

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:17.789
This is your apartment!

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:20.550
Oh yeah right.

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:23.189
So why are we playing Truth or Dare though?

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.470
For views.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:27.679
Ok, good enough for me.

00:00:27.679 --> 00:00:29.140
So what will it be then?

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.939
Truth or Dare?

00:00:31.939 --> 00:00:32.939
Dare obviously.

00:00:32.939 --> 00:00:38.390
I dare you, to find me 19 Things You Missed
in the new movie Truth or Dare.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.390
I mean...

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:44.180
I was gonna do that anyway.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.100
Many of the first things you missed stem from
the first Truths and Dares when Carter / Sam

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.590
takes them to the mission to trick them into
joining the game.

00:00:50.590 --> 00:00:54.170
I'll come back to Olivia's truth question
later in this video because it leads into

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:55.890
a bigger point I that want to make.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.410
But many of the questions that the friends
ask each other are teasers into the cause

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:00.660
of their untimely deaths.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:06.122
For example, Ronnie is challenged to lap dance
a guy, and we he his hesitation to do a dare

00:01:06.122 --> 00:01:07.840
that makes him look bad.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:13.130
Later on, at the pub when Calyx is one daring
him, his hesitation leads to his own demise.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:16.480
Lucas's dare is to go nude in front of everyone,
which represents him making himself sexually

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:18.150
available to more than one person.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:26.180
He meets his fate when he's unable to choose
which girl he has feelings for.

00:01:26.180 --> 00:01:28.360
Then Brad is dared to make out with someone.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:32.480
He chooses a guy, which sets up his confrontation
with his father who is against homosexuality.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:37.070
This encounter sets up tension between the
police officer and his son puts the other

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.910
cops on high alert about Brad.

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:42.750
In the end, one of the cops pulls the trigger
on him too soon.

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:46.890
Then we've got Tyson who has to tell the truth
about forging prescriptions to freshman.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:50.560
He's basically asked the same question by
Calyx, only this time it's in front of someone

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:51.680
who's interviewing him.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:55.640
He lies, and as a result, Calyx makes him
stab himself in the face.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:02.540
There's been a lot of that in movies lately,
huh?

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:07.390
And the last member of the group is Penelope.

00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:10.750
It's not so much the dare that exposes her
weakness here, but the fact that she's super

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.200
drunk when she does it.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.030
It's later mentioned that she has a bit of
an issue with day drinking, so her dare shows

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.560
her the consequences of alcohol by making
her walk the edge of the roof.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:24.060
It's important to note that she would have
died here if they didn't catch her, but it

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:29.090
didn't really matter because she ends up getting
shot like 4 minutes later so...

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:31.640
I honestly don't get what the point of that
was.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.560
But the main theme to take away from Penelope
is that she gets drunk all the time and it

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.080
causes her to do things she might not normally
do.

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:40.930
I'm also going to talk about how Calyx's game
maybe wasn't entirely a curse and could have

00:02:40.930 --> 00:02:45.380
actually been a blessing in disguise and helped
the group, but first let's talk about some

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.520
Easter Eggs.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:50.570
Truth or Dare has a lot in common with another
recent Blumhouse movie, Happy Death Day.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:54.870
Did anyone notice that the layout of the sorority
house in this movie was the exact same as

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.610
the one in Happy Death Day?

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:01.120
Now it could just be that all sorority houses
are laid out like this.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.080
I wouldn't know because I went to art school
and probably wouldn't have been invited to

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:08.569
their parties even if I had gone to a university,
but regardless, I'd say there's a pretty good

00:03:08.569 --> 00:03:11.860
chance that they reused that Happy Death Day
set for Truth or Dare.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:16.210
I also thought that the skull logo seen during
many of the dares that's supposed to represent

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.870
Calyx looked a lot like Bughuul from Sinister.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:22.700
I know Jason Blum has talked recently about
the possibility of a Blumhouse crossover,

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:26.800
so maybe these films take place in the same
universe.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.170
And one more Easter Egg I caught was the character
Carter.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.440
Or I guess his real name is Sam.

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:35.030
There's a good chance he was inspired by Hugh
from the movie It Follows.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.500
The next 20 seconds have spoilers for It Follows.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.010
They both pretend to be interested in the
lead girl in order to get their gaurds down

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:44.920
and trick them into joining the curse, which
really only buys some time until it's their

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:45.920
turn again.

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:50.800
They both use fake names, abandoned locations,
and both go into hiding after passing off

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:51.910
the curse.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.280
Outside of the connections to other movies,
there are also some cool visual references

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.550
within the movie.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.190
In the living room there's a giant 6 sided
die.

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:03.060
Not including Carter, who isn't really actually
part of the friend group, there are 6 people

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.060
in the group.

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:15.430
And after Ronnie's death, when they are discussing
it the number 5 faces 

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:16.430
the camera.

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:19.739
In the med building where Tyson had the interview,
a sign in the background talks about a Whooping

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:20.739
Cough outbreak.

00:04:20.739 --> 00:04:25.080
I had to look this up after the movie, but
it's essentially a disease that's highly contagious,

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:27.139
but easily treated with modern medicine.

00:04:27.139 --> 00:04:29.830
To me, that's kind of like the truth or dare
game itself.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:33.800
Highly contagious because it's easy to get
other people involved, but easy to treat if

00:04:33.800 --> 00:04:35.600
you have no secrets to hide.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.669
That's one of the reasons I think the game
could be a blessing in a way, rather than

00:04:38.669 --> 00:04:39.669
a curse.

00:04:39.669 --> 00:04:43.350
All of the truth questions could help make
the character being asked a better person.

00:04:43.350 --> 00:04:46.410
And if you've got nothing to hide, you've
got nothing to worry about.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:50.770
The dares seem to prey on your biggest flaws,
as I've already mentioned, so by making yourself

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:54.810
a better, more honest person you'd be less
prone to dares.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.180
Except for Brad.

00:04:56.180 --> 00:04:58.500
He just kind of gets screwed over in the end.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:02.300
Maybe there's something I'm missing with him,
but he also does kind of prove the point that

00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:06.050
the game can improve your life, because when
Calyx forces him to come out of closet to

00:05:06.050 --> 00:05:10.180
his father, he actually talks about how good
it felt to finally have that off his chest.

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:13.850
I actually think it would have fit the theme
of the movie better if he has ended up surviving

00:05:13.850 --> 00:05:17.500
in the end as an example of someone who improved
their life by putting everything out on the

00:05:17.500 --> 00:05:18.500
table.

00:05:18.500 --> 00:05:21.571
If you look at any of the characters, they
could have avoided big issues if they had

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:23.150
been more honest with each other.

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:26.870
If Markee wasn't cheating on her boyfriend
she never would have had an issue and the

00:05:26.870 --> 00:05:29.150
whole fued with Olivia would have been avoided.

00:05:29.150 --> 00:05:32.730
And on the contrary if Lucas was honest that
he wasn't sure about Markee, then he never

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:35.150
would have had to cheat on her with Olivia.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:39.530
And as a little side note, during that scene,
Markee says she'd rather be anywhere but here

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:41.460
and goes to a little Tortas stand.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:47.820
So she decides to get Mexican food after the
root of all get problems just started in Mexico.

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:50.110
You think she'd maybe try something else.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:53.710
And then of course there's the big reveal
about how Olivia was there during Markee's

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:57.880
father's suicide, which is actually kind of
fair because she only kept that from Markee

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:02.040
to protect her and there was no reason to
make her think badly of her deceased Dad.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.200
Overall, Olivia is the most honest and caring
person, so she is able to survive the game,

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.200
for now at least.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.720
But there is actually one big lie that Olivia
tells, and it's the thing I mentioned way

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.110
at the beginning of the movie.

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:15.520
So they had just had their Spring Break trip,
they don't want the night to end after partying

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:18.800
in Mexico, and this guy Carter leads them
to the abandoned mission to play Truth or

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:19.800
Dare.

00:06:19.800 --> 00:06:23.220
Brad is still drunk at the time and asks Olivia
an oddly specific question.

00:06:23.220 --> 00:06:27.820
He asks, if Aliens invaded Mexico and she
had to choose between saving the friend group

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:31.130
and saving the rest of Mexico what would she
choose?

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:34.620
Everyone thinks she's going to save the group,
including her best friend.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:39.310
We are given the idea that she values the
lives of many over her own.

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:43.250
However, at the end of the movie, she is faced
with essentially the same scenario.

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:47.670
She can let her and Markee die, and end the
game once and for all, or she can challenge

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:53.479
the entirety of her YouTube audience and endanger
the lives of her 4.5K subscribers, or let's

00:06:53.479 --> 00:06:56.820
face it, with the current state of broken
YouTube notifications, more like 200 people

00:06:56.820 --> 00:06:58.639
would actually be in danger.

00:06:58.639 --> 00:06:59.639
But still!

00:06:59.639 --> 00:07:00.760
She chooses the subscribers!

00:07:00.760 --> 00:07:02.240
She makes the selfish choice.

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:05.490
At the beginning of the movie she's this caring
person who wants to build homes for people

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:08.940
and save strangers over herself, but at the
end she does just the opposite.

00:07:08.940 --> 00:07:13.280
I don't know if that is a result of her ideals
changing to become more selfish, or if she

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:16.280
was just lying to herself and her friends
at the beginning.

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:20.830
But whatever the answer may be, there's one
thing about this movie that I find disgusting.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:25.860
The fact that this supposed YouTuber, sells
out her subscribers lives for her own gain.

00:07:25.860 --> 00:07:29.900
I may be kind of twisted, but I would NEVER
do that to you people.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:32.415
First of all, if you kill off your subscribers,
your views are going to go down.

00:07:32.415 --> 00:07:38.020
And secondly, you're supposed to treat your
subscribers like royalty, by delivering quality

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:41.669
content and having engaging discussions in
the comments!

00:07:41.669 --> 00:07:42.669
You know what?

00:07:42.669 --> 00:07:44.830
It's no wonder she only has 4.5K subscribers.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:46.110
She treats them like crap.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.630
We only see her post once during the course
of this film, which takes place from Spring

00:07:49.630 --> 00:07:53.789
Break, which is usually in March or April,
to at least June 7th, which is shown as the

00:07:53.789 --> 00:07:56.410
date on Olivia's phone like 3/4th of the way
through the movie.

00:07:56.410 --> 00:07:58.229
And then it actually goes past that.

00:07:58.229 --> 00:08:00.720
So that's like 3-4 months without posting.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:05.290
I mean there IS a demon trying to kill her,
but if it was me, I'm just saying I wouldn't

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.410
miss an upload.

00:08:06.410 --> 00:08:10.190
I mean there's no excuse for this girl to
be that attractive, and not have close to

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:11.250
a million subs.

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:15.530
Your content can literally be terrible if
you look good, and as long as you post often,

00:08:15.530 --> 00:08:16.530
you'll make it.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.660
It's been proven time and time again.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.580
The rest of us have to work hard.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:24.380
And do I sometimes ask you to follow me on
Twitter, Facebook and Instagram?

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:25.380
Yeah.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:27.759
Do I ask you to like this video if you enjoyed
the content?

00:08:27.759 --> 00:08:28.759
Sure.

00:08:28.759 --> 00:08:32.469
Do I put links to my merch and ask you to
consider supporting the channel by picking

00:08:32.469 --> 00:08:34.249
up one of these cool designs?

00:08:34.249 --> 00:08:35.309
Sometimes I do.

00:08:35.309 --> 00:08:39.469
But have I ever, done something to put your
life in danger?

00:08:39.469 --> 00:08:40.469
No.

00:08:40.469 --> 00:08:43.860
And when I say assuming we both survive at
the end of every video, I at least kind of

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:47.589
hope that you actually do, because I do love
seeing your input in the comments.

00:08:47.589 --> 00:08:48.589
You know what?

00:08:48.589 --> 00:08:49.589
I don't like this Olivia character.

00:08:49.589 --> 00:08:51.130
What a bad YouTuber.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:54.510
Because I actually care about my fans, I'm
going to offer you this.

00:08:54.510 --> 00:08:58.759
Leave your own Truths and Dares in the comments
and I'll take the highest rated ones and make

00:08:58.759 --> 00:09:01.450
a video answering the truths and doing the
dares.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:03.290
I have just 3 rules.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:04.949
I won't do anything illegal.

00:09:04.949 --> 00:09:06.559
I won't delete any content.

00:09:06.559 --> 00:09:08.820
And I won't spend a bunch of my own money.

00:09:08.820 --> 00:09:11.959
In return, my only dare for you is this.

00:09:11.959 --> 00:09:17.279
I dare you to subscribe to CZsWorld for new
horrors every week, ring that deathbell for

00:09:17.279 --> 00:09:20.920
notifications and I'll see you in the next
one.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.470
Assuming, we both survive.

